+For Word, Excel, and PowerPoint generation, first call `office_workspace` with `action: "create"`. Put the `.univer` file, authoring scripts, assets, screenshots, rendered pages, reports, and draft exports inside its returned directory. Temporary directories such as `/tmp` may be isolated per command or tool; the returned directory is shared across calls. Do not write intermediates directly into the desktop or workspace root. If `office_workspace` is unavailable, allocate one unique temporary subdirectory under the current session workspace and clean only that directory after copying final deliverables out.
+
+Complete the required content checks and visual review while the temporary files still exist, and wait for every authoring/rendering process to exit. Export into the temporary directory, then call `office_workspace` with `action: "finish"`, its `directory`, and `files: [{ source, destination }]` for only the requested final files. The tool publishes new files without replacing existing destinations and removes all intermediates. Present only its returned final paths. Keep `.univer` sources or previews only when explicitly requested; never move user originals into temporary storage. Before waiting for user choices across turns, call `office_workspace` action `pause`; call `resume` with the same directory on the next turn. Paused projects survive a normal waiting turn. Other temporary directories expire at the end of the current turn, including errors and cancellation. Finish before ending the turn, or call `discard` to abandon the draft. Do not leave background processes writing there.
